# LIQUID-09 — Break loops early when a match is found

## Rationale

When a loop searches for one matching value to assign, continuing after a match
wastes iterations. Liquid supports `{% break %}` inside loops.

## How to check

Look for `{% for %}` blocks that assign inside `{% if %}` on first match but lack
`{% break %}` after the assignment.

## How to fix

Add `{% break %}` immediately after the assignment when the match is found. Or
replace the loop with an array filter (see LIQUID-11).

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% assign current_color_value = '' %}
{% assign color_option_values = product.options_with_values[color_index].values %}
{% for value in color_option_values %}
  {% if value.name == current_color %}
    {% assign current_color_value = value.swatch.color.rgb %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% assign current_color_value = '' %}
{% assign color_option_values = product.options_with_values[color_index].values %}
{% for value in color_option_values %}
  {% if value.name == current_color %}
    {% assign current_color_value = value.swatch.color.rgb %}
    {% break %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
```
